<title>MEXICO: Mexico's nominal GDP 2.439 billion pesos in Q3.</title>
<headline>Mexico's nominal GDP 2.439 billion pesos in Q3.</headline>
<dateline>MEXICO CITY 1996-11-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>Mexico's gross domestic product at market prices was 2.439 billion current pesos in the third quarter, and the implicit price deflator was 29.3 percent compared with the same period last year, the National Statistics Institute said on Tuesday.</p>
<p>It reaffirmed data released last week in showing the economy grew 7.4 percent in Q3 from the July-September period of 1995.  </p>
<p>It released the following data on nominal GDP:</p>
<p>Sector	    Amount in current prices	   Percentage</p>
<p>			     million pesos	    of total nominal GDP</p>
<p>Farming,</p>
<p>Forestry and Fishing     120,713			5.4 pct</p>
<p>Industrial:		  687,225		     30.6 pct</p>
<p>  Mining			34,594			1.5 pct</p>
<p>  Manufacturing	    505,678		     22.5 pct</p>
<p>  Construction	     111,316			5.0 pct</p>
<p>  Power Generation</p>
<p>  Electricity, Gas, Water 35,637			1.6 pct</p>
<p>Commerce, Restaurants,</p>
<p>Hotels			 451,148		     20.1 pct</p>
<p>Services		     984,620		     43.9 pct</p>
<p>--Cecilia Cardenas, Mexico City newsroom +525 728-9552</p>
